$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,2-Dimethyl-1-phenyl-pent-4-en-1-ol Magnesium turnings (0.96 g, 40 mmol)
were mixed with Et2O (20 mL) and bromo benzene (4.71 g, 0.030 mol) in
Et2O (15 mL) was slowly added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1 h and then heated to reflux for another 30 min. Then a
solution of 2,2-dimethyl pent-4-enal (2.35 g, 0.021 mol) in Et2O (10 mL)
was slowly added and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 2 h.
Ice (10 g) was added and the resulting suspension was dissolved with HCl
(2 M). The organic layer was separated, washed with aqueous NaHSO3,
aqueous NaHCO3 and H2O, and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent and
distillation at reduced pressure (bp. 77 °C / 0.9 mbar) afforded the
desired product as a colourless liquid (3.75 g, 94 %).
2,2-Dimethyl-1-phenyl-pent-4-en-1-ol, yield (3.75 g, 94 %). IR (neat):
3452s, 3070m, 2969s, 2874w, 1953w, 1818w, 1639w, 1452m, 1385m, 1292m,
1190m, 1084w, 1038s, 914s, 784w, 742s, 703s cm-1. 1H-NMR (300 MHz): δ =
7.33-7.30 (m, 5 H, aryl-H), 5.92 (tdd, J1 =15.8 Hz, J2 =11.4 Hz, J3 = 7.5
Hz, 1 H, CH2=CH), 5.11-5.04 (m, 2 H, CH=CH2), 4.47 (s, 1 H, HCO), 2.20
(dd, J1 = 13.5 Hz, J2 = 7.6 Hz, 1 H, CH2), 2.03 (dd, J1 = 13.5 Hz, J2 =
7.4 Hz, 1 H, CH2), 1.85 (br s, 1 H, OH), 0.91 (s, 3 H, CH3), 0.84 (s, 3
H, CH3). 13C-NMR (75 MHz): δ = 141.8 (C), 135.4 (CH), 127.8 (CH), 127.6
(CH), 127.3 (CH), 117.3 (CH2), 80.9 (CH), 43.5 (CH2), 38.5 (C),
23.4(CH3), 22.2(CH3). MS (EI): m/z = 190 ([M]+). HRMS (ESI): m/z =
[M+Na]+ Calcd for C13H18ONa: 213.1255, Found: 213.1250. Anal. Calcd. For
C13H18O (190.28): C, 82.06; H, 9.53. Found: C, 81.84; H, 9.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
