$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(2-Hydroxy)phenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1f)6 Following the
Representative Procedure, 2-hydroxybenzaldehyde (122 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (163 μL, 1.5
mmol, 1.5 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 35 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 48 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/MTBE (4:1, 300 mL) provided 1f (132
mg, 81%) as a yellow oil. 1-(2-Hydroxy)phenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1f)6, yield
132 mg, 81%. Data for 1f: 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.03 (br, 1 H, (OH)),
7.17 (td, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1 H, Aryl), 6.97 (dd, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1 H, Aryl),
6.89-6.82 (m, 2 H, Aryl), 5.90-5.79 (m, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.26-5.19 (m, 2 H,
H2C(4)), 4.87 (dd, J = 8.4, 5.6, 1 H, HC(1)), 2.81 (br, 1 H, HO),
2.68-2.54 m, 2 H, H2C(2)) 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 155.5 (C(2')), 133.8
(C(3)), 129.0 (C(4')), 127.1 (C(6')), 126.2 (C(1')), 119.8 (C(5')), 119.4
(C(3')), 117.2 (C(4)), 74.6 (C(1)), 42.1 (C(2)) IR: (NaCl) 3337 (s), 3071
(s), 2976 (m), 2928 (m), 1640 (m), 1609 (m), 1587 (s), 1490 (s), 1456
(s), 1384 (m), 1349 (m), 1240 (s)HRMS: (ESI) Calcd. for C10H12O2Na,
187.0735; found, 187.0740 TLC: Rf 0.32 (hexanes/EtOAc, 3/1) [UV, CAM]
