$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM As illustrated in Scheme 4, hydroboration of (P)-4 with (dIpc)2BH at -20
&#x00B0;C for 8 h followed by addition of benzaldehyde at -78 &#x00B0;C
provided homoallylic alcohol 6a in 80% yield and 95% ee. In contrast,
when the identical reaction conditions were used for the hydroboration of
the enantiomeric allene (M)-4 with (dIpc)2BH, ketone 8 was obtained in
75% yield along with 6% of alcohol 6a, obtained with 72% ee. 6a:
[&#x3B1;]D26.8 = -83.8&#x00B0; (c 1.15, CHCl3); 95% ee; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) &#x3B4; 7.27-7.49 (m, 10H), 6.12 (dd, J = 18.8, 7.6 Hz, 1H), 5.94
(d, J = 18.4 Hz, 1H), 4.42 (dd, J = 7.6, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.52-2.57 (m, 1H),
2.07 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H), 0.90 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.35 (s, 6H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4; 150.5, 142.7, 139.0, 134.1, 130.9, 129.3, 128.5,
128.1, 127.9, 127.1, 78.1, 49.2, 16.6, -2.14, -2.17; IR (neat) 3400,
3067, 2959, 2929, 1614, 1493, 1453, 1427, 1327, 1247, 1112, 1070, 1022,
998, 843, 822, 731, 699 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z for C19H24OSiNa [M+Na]+
calcd 319.1494, found 319.1500.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown,
(1S,2S,E)-4-(dimethyl(phenyl)silyl)-2-methyl-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol, 72%
ee
