$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Naphthalen-2-yl-but-2-en-1-ol: To 1.2 g (49 mol) of mechanically
activated Mg(0) was added 15 mL of THF and I2 (cat., in 0.5 mL of THF).
Initiation was afforded by brief warming with a heatgun (brown ??
clear/white color shift), after which 0.010 kg (48 mmol) of
2-bromonapthalene in 10 mL of THF was carefully added over 30 min to
maintain a gentle reflux. The mixture was refluxed 15 min longer with a
heatgun, then stirred at ambient temperature for 1 h. In a separate
flask, 4.8 mL (4.1 g) of crotonaldehyde was dissolved in 19 mL of THF and
the temperature reduced to -78°C. The active Grignard reagent was added
via syringe over 15 min and after 1 h, the reaction was quenched
carefully with sat. aq. NH4Cl and raised to ambient temperature. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3x), the combined organic layers
were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and the crude product mixture was
concentrated in vacuo. The product was purified by flash chromatography
on SiO2 (6:1 hexanes/EtOAc) to give as a highly viscous, yellow oil
1-Naphthalen-2-yl-but-2-en-1-ol, yield 7.5 g, 79%. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.86-7.82 (m, 4H), 7.51-7.45 (m, 3H), 5.90-5.73 (m, 2H), 5.35
(d, J = 5.1 Hz, 1H), 2.00 (s, 1H), 1.76 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Strategies for Expanding Structural Diversity Available from Olefin
Isomerization-Claisen Rearrangement Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stevens, Benjamin D.; Bungard, Christopher J.; Nelson, Scott G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(17), 6397-6402

