$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(4R,5R,E)-4-Methyl-7-phenyl-hepta-2-ene-4,5-diol (2a). Crystalline
(dIpc)2BH (118 mg, 0.41 mmol) was weighed into a round bottom flask
containing a stir bar in a glove box. (Note: The crystalline borane
should be crushed and pulverized to fine powder with a glass rod in order
to ensure efficient hydroboration). The flask was capped with a rubber
septum, removed from the glove box and placed in a cold bath. Toluene (2
mL) was added to the flask and the mixture (suspension) was cooled to -25
°C. Allenylboronate (168 mg, 0.87 mmol) in toluene (1 mL) was added
dropwise. This mixture was stirred for 5h at -25 °C, then cooled to -78
°C and freshly distilled hydrocinnamaldehyde (44 μL, 0.33 mmol) was added
at -78 °C dropwise to the reaction mixture via microliter syringe. The
mixture was stirred for 4h at -78 °C, then MeOH (1 mL) and THF (1 mL)
were added. The mixture was allowed to warm to 0 °C and then 3 N NaOH (2
mL) was added followed by slow addition of 50% H2O2 (2 mL) at 0 °C. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at room temperature, then was
diluted with saturated NaHCO3 and brine and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic extracts were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the
crude product by flash chromatography (hexane : EtOAc = 5 : 1 to 4:1)
provided diol 2a. (4R,5R,E)-4-Methyl-7-phenyl-hepta-2-ene-4,5-diol
(2a).Yield 88%; (4R,5S,E)-4-Methyl-7-phenyl-hepta-2-ene-3,4-diol (3a).
Yield 88%. 2a: [α ]D 28.0 = +38.3° (c 0.52, CHCl3); 90% ee; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.24-7.29 (m, 2H), 7.18-7.21 (m, 3H), 5.72 (dq, J = 15.6,
6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.33 (dq, J = 15.6, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 3.40 (dd, J = 10.4, 2.1 Hz,
1H), 2.92 (m, 1H), 2.62 (ddd, J = 13.7, 9.7, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 2.43 (brs, 1H),
2.19 (brs, 1H), 1.74-1.82 (m, 1H), 1.70 (dd, J = 10.4, 2.1 Hz, 3H),
1.59-1.72 (m, 1H), 1.20 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.2, 135.3,
128.5, 128.4, 125.9, 125.8, 76.8, 75.1, 32.9, 32.8, 21.5, 17.9; IR (neat)
3417, 2928, 1604, 1497, 1455, 1378, 1063, 973, 749, 700 cm-1; HRMS (ESI)
m/z for C14H2OO2Na [M+Na]+ calcd 243.1361, found 243.1359. 3a: [α ]D 28.0
= -5.0° (c 0.40 , CHCl3); anti:syn = 7:1; 87% ee; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.27-7.31 (m, 2H), 7.17-7.22 (m, 3H), 5.73 (dq, J = 15.6, 6.4 Hz, 1H),
5.55 (dq, J = 15.6, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 3.42 (dd, J = 10.7, 2.0 Hz, 1H),
2.92-2.89 (m, 1H), 2.65 (ddd, J = 13.7, 9.7, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 2.23 (brs, 2H),
2.19 (brs, 1H), 1.78-1.86 (m, 1H), 1.72 (dd, J = 6.4, 1.5 Hz, 3H),
1.55-1.65 (m, 1H), 1.25 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.1, 133.3,
128.5, 128.4, 125.9, 125.8, 77.7, 76.7, 75.1, 33.8, 32.9, 32.8, 24.6,
17.9; IR (neat) 3415, 3027, 2929, 1604, 1497, 1456, 1378, 1058, 973, 752,
700 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z for C14H2OO2Na [M+Na]+ calcd 243.1361, found
243.1363.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, yield depends on borane used in stage 1,
alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield, alternative preparation
shown, product ratio and ee depends on borane used in stage 1, in-situ
generated reactant (1st and 2nd stage)
