$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(R)-5-chloromethyl-1-phenyl-hex-5-en-3-ol. To a 50 mL round-bottom flask
were added oven dried 4Å molecular sieves (890 mg, 400 mg/mmol of
aldehyde), (S)-BINOL (140 mg, 0.489 mmol, 0.22 eq), CH2Cl2 (8.90 mL, 0.25
M), titanium(IV) isopropoxide (1.00 M solution in CH2Cl2, 245 μL,
245μmol, 0.11 eq) and trifluoroacetic acid (freshly prepared 0.10 M
solution in CH2Cl2, 78 μL, 7.7 μmol, 3.5 x 10-3 eq). The flask was
equipped with a reflux condenser, and the red-brown mixture was heated at
40 °C. After 2 h the mixture was cooled to room temperature and the
reflux condenser exchanged for a rubber septum. Hydrocinnamaldehyde (293
μL, 2.23 mmol, 1.00 eq) was added, the mixture stirred for 30 min and
then cooled to -78 °C. Tributyl-(2-chloromethyl-allyl)-stannane (959 μL,
2.89 mmol, 1.30 eq) was added, the mixture stirred for 30 min and the
flask placed in a freezer at -20 °C. After 72 h the mixture was removed
from the freezer, and a saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (15 mL) was
added. The mixture was stirred for 30 min, allowed to settle and then
filtered through a plug of Celite®. The organic phase was diluted with
CH2Cl2 (50 mL) and washed with water (2 x 25 mL) and brine (20 mL). The
organic phase was dried over Na2SO4, filtered, concentrated under reduced
pressure, and purified by flash chromatography on a 4.5 x 18 cm silica
gel column eluting with a solvent gradient from 2.5% (600 mL) through 5%
(1500 mL), 7.5% (1000 mL) and 10% EtOAc/hexanes (1000 mL). The eluant was
collected in 30 mL portions and the product containing fractions (30 to
67) were concentrated and combined. Preparation of
(S)-3-chloromethyl-1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol as a clear colorless oil, yield
613mg, 3.12 mmol, 98%. Rf 0.38 (25% EtOAc/hexanes); [α]20D -42.9 (c =
1.190, CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.40 - 7.36 (m, 3H), 7.33 - 7.30
(m, 2H), 5.29 (s, 1H), 5.11 (d, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H), 4.89 (dd, J = 9.0, 4.3
Hz, 1H), 4.10 (dd, J = 11.8, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 4.07 (dd, J = 11.8, 0.9 Hz,
1H), 2.66 (dd, J = 14.6, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 2.59 (dd, J = 14.4, 0.8 Hz, 1H),
2.13 (s, 1H); 125 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 144.0, 142.1, 128.7 (2), 128.0,
125.9 (2), 118.0, 72.7, 48.4, 43.3; 125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH2: 118.0,
48.4, 43.3. CH: 128.7 (2), 128.0, 125.9 (2), 72.7. C: 144.0, 142.1; IR
(neat) 3550, 3392 (bs), 3084, 3063, 3030, 2947, 2920, 1645, 1603, 1493,
1453, 1401, 1360, 1309, 1258, 1201, 1081, 1052, 1018, 914, 885, 857, 757,
701, 673, 631 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C11H13OCl: C, 67.18; H, 6.66. Found:
C, 67.13; H, 6.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used first stage
