$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(E)-5-Methyl-7-(trimethylsilyl)hepta-1,4-dien-6-yn-3- General Procedure
for the Addition of Grignard Reagents to Aldehydes 9a and 9b. To a
solution of the aldehyde (5.4 mmol) in ether (20 mL) cooled to 0 °C was
added dropwise the correspondent Grignard reagent (vinylmagnesium bromide
or allylmagnesium bromide) (6.5 mL, 1 M solution in THF, 6.5 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred for 10 min at 0 °C. Then, a saturated
aqueous solution of NH4-Cl (5 mL) was added, and the aqueous mixture was
extracted with EtOAc (3 X 10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with brine (10 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The resulting oil was purified by column
chromatography. (E)-6-Phenyl-8-(trimethylsilyl)octa-1,5-dien-7-yn-4-ol
(13b). Prepared from enyne 9b. Obtained as a colourless oil in 90%
yield,. Rf = 0.25 (Hex:EtOAc 10:1) KMnO4. 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz):
7.46-7.37 (m; 5H), 6.21 (d, 3J = 9.7; 1H), 5.83-5.71 (m; 1H), 5.22-5.12
(m; 2H), 4.40-4.28 (m; 1H), 2.45-2.31 (m; 2H), 0.21 (s; 9H). 13C-NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz): 140.1 (C), 136.5 (C), 133.4 (CH), 128.6 (CH), 128.1
(CH), 126.1 (CH), 118.7 (CH2), 118.3 (C), 105.8 (C), 94.4 (C), 67.3 (CH),
41.6 (CH2), -0.1 (CH3). HRMS (EI) calcd for C17H22OSi-C3H5 229.1050,
found 229.1040.
