$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(3R,4S)-(+)-3-Methyl-1-trimethylsilyl-1-decyn-5-en-4-ol (31).Standard
Procedure for Allenylindium Additions. A flame-dried flask was charged
with THF (3 mL) and HMPA (1 mL). trans-2- Heptenal (74 mg, 0.66 mmol, 1
equiv) was then added followed by Pd(OAc)2 (9.8 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.06
equiv) and PPh3 (12.2 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.06 equiv). Upon complete
dissolution of the PPh3, the solution was cooled to 0 °C. TIPS mesylate
(S)-1c (247 mg, 0.81 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added to the solution followed
by InI powder (258 mg, 1.1 mmol, 1.6 equiv). The mixture was then stirred
at 0 °C for 15 min before being warmed to rt. After 1 h, the reaction
mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (20 mL) and
extracted with Et2O. The Et2O solution was separated, dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography to yield alcohol 31 (159 mg, 75% yield,
80:20 mixture of anti and syn diastereomer separable by flash
chromatography with 20% Et2Ohexanes elutant) as a clear oil:
(3R,4S,5E)-(-)-l-(triisopropylsilyl)-3,6,10-trimethyl-5,9-undecadiene-l-yn-4-ol(32).
The standard procedure for allenylindium addition was employed with THF
(3 mL), HMPA (1 mL), aldehyde 24 (101.5 mg, 0.66 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (9.6 mg,
0.04 mmol), PPh3 (10.9 mg, 0.04 mmol), TIPSmesylate (S)-lc (246.7 mg,
0.81 mmol) and InI powder (260.7 mg, 1.07 mmol) affording alcohol 32 (184
mg, 76% yield, 67:33 mixture of anti and syn diastereomers separable by
flash chromatography with 20% Et2O/hexanes elutant) as a clear oil: [α]20
D = +13.0 (c 3.67, CHCl3); IR (film) 3403, 2954, 2864, 2161, 1462 cm-1;
1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 5.23-5.26(m, 1H), 5.09-5.13 (m, 1H), 4.16-4.21 (m, 1H),
2.53-2.62 (m, 1H), 2.05-2.14 (m, 4H), 1.73 (s, 3H), 1.70 (s, 3H), 1.62
(s, 3H), 1.19 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.10 (s, 21H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ
140.5, 131.6, 124.9, 123.9, 109.8, 83.1, 71.3, 39.6, 35.3, 26.2, 25.6,
18.6, 17.6, 17.0, 16.9, 11.1; Anal. Calcd. for C23H42OSi: C 76.17, H
11.67; Found: C 76.42, H 11.76.
