$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure VII: Aldol Addition of
(Z)-24 and 25: (1R, 2R, 4S)-5-tert-
Butyldimethylsilyloxy-2,4-dimethyl-1-hydroxy-1-phenyl-3-pentanone
(syn,syn-45a)In a 10-mL Schlenk flask was placed a solution of (R,R)-1
(37 mg, 0.10 mmol, 0.10 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL). To the solution was
added (Z)-24 (364 mg, 1.00 mmol) and the solution was cooled to -70 °C
using an acetone/CO2 bath. To the solution was added dropwise PhCHO (102
μL, 1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) and the reaction mixture was stirred for 6 h at
-70 °C. The reaction mixture was quenched by pouring into a vigorously
stirring cold saturated NaHCO3 aq (5 mL). The resulting slurry was
stirred for 1 h and filtered through Celite. The layers were separated,
and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 10 mL). The combined
organic extrates were washed with brine (5 mL), dried over sodium sulfate
and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified
by column chromatography (silica gel, pentane/ether, 3/1, 30 mm) to
afford 241 mg (0.72 mmol, 72%) of 45a as a clear viscous oil. (2S, 4R,
5R)-1-Triisopropylsilyloxy-2,4,6-trimethyl-5-hydroxy-6-octen-3-one
(syn,syn-46g), yield 85%. 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 5.60 (qt, J = 6.8,
1.5, 1 H, HC(7)); 4.42 (m, 1 H, HC(5)); 3.87-3.67 (ABX, 2 H, H2C(1));
3.11 (d, J = 2.5, 1 H, HO); 3.02 (sext, J = 6.8, 1 H, HC(2)); 2.88 (qd, J
= 7.3, 2.9, 1 H, HC(4)); 1.63 (d, J = 6.3, 3 H, H3C(8)); 1.56 (s, 3 H,
H3C(13)); 1.10 - 1.02 (m, 27 H, H3C(11), H3C(10), H3C(12), HC(9)) 13C
NMR: (126 MHz, CDCl3) 219.2 (C(3)); 133.7 (C(7)); 119.9 (C(6)); 73.8
(C(1)); 66.5 (C(5)); 48.6 (C(4)); 47.5 (C(2)); 17.9 (C(10)); 13.4 (C(8));
13.3 (C(13)); 12.9 (C(11)); 11.8 (C(9)); 9.0 (C(12)) IR: (CHCl3) 3584
(br, w); 2945 (m); 2868 (m); 1701 (w); 1461 (w); 1383 (w); 1103 (w) MS:
(FI) 357 (M+, 7); 311 (5); 310 (4); 231 (5); 230 (18); 229 (100) Opt.
Rot.: [α]D24 + 5.71 (EtOH, c = 0.20) TLC: Rf 0.20 (pentane/ether, 5/1)
[silica gel, p-anisaldehyde] Analysis: C20H40O3Si (356.62) Calcd: C,
67.36%; H, 11.31% Found: C, 66.99%; H, 11.28%
