$DATUM (E)-1-(2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)phenyl)butan-1-ol (11b). 1-Bromopropane
(886 mg, 7.2 mmol) was added so slowly to a mixture of Mg (182 mg, 7.5
mmol) in THF (10 ml) that the mixture was kept mild refluxing. After
addition, the mixture was stirred for 2 h. To a solution of
(E)-2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)benzaldehyde (10a) (486 mg, 3 mmol) in THF
(10 ml) was added a solution of above Grignard reagent (7.2 mmol) at room
temperature. The reaction solution was stirred for 10 h under refluxing.
After the reaction was cooled to 0 °C, an aqueous saturated solution of
NH4Cl (20 ml) was added dropwise and the resulting mixture was stirred
for 10 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with diethyl ether (30 mL ×
3). The combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuum. The crude residue was purified by chromatography
on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 1/1). The product 11b as yellowish
oil (483 mg, 78% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.91 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
3H), 1.25-1.50 (m, 2H), 1.64-1.77 (m, 2H), 2.16 (br, 2H), 4.97 (dd, J =
5.6 Hz, 1.6 Hz, 2H), 4.30 (dd, J = 8.0 Hz, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 6.16-6.23 (m,
1H), 6.93 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 7.23-7.29 (m, 2H), 7.41-7.46 (m, 2H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.0, 19.1, 40.2, 63.6, 70.6, 125.6, 126.5,
127.4, 127.8, 127.9, 131.1, 134.8, 141.7; MS (EI) m/z (rel) 163 (19), 145
(47), 131 (12), 129 (12), 118 (12), 117 (100), 115 (45), 91 (21); HRMS
for C13H18O2: 206.1307; Found: 206.1304; IR (film): 3312 (br), 3217 (br),
2920 (m), 1452 (s), 1058 (s), 1029 (s), 960 (s), 743 (s) cm-1.
