$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(4R,5S,E)-4-Methyl-7-phenyl-hepta-2-ene-3,4-diol (3a). Crystalline
(dIpc)2BH (60 mg,0.21 mmol) was weighed into a round bottom flask
containing a stir bar in a glove box. (Note: The crystalline borane
should be crushed and pulverized to fine powder with a glass rod in order
to ensure efficient hydroboration). The flask was capped with a rubber
septum and removed from the glove box and placed in a cold bath. Toluene
(0.5 mL) was added to the flask and the mixture (suspension) was cooled
to -25 °C. Allenylboronate (85 mg, 0.44 mmol) in toluene (0.5 mL) was
added dropwise, and the mixture was stirred for 5h at -25 °C. The clear
solution was then stirred at 95 °C for 1.5h and then cooled to -78 °C.
Freshly distilled hydrocinnamaldehyde (22 μL, 0.17 mmol) was added at -78
°C dropwise to the reaction mixture via microliter syringe. The mixture
was stirred for 4h at -78 °C, then MeOH (0.5 mL) and THF (0.5 mL) were
added. The mixture was allowed to warm to 0 °C and then 3 N NaOH (1 mL)
was added followed by slow addition of 50% H2O2 (1 mL). The reaction
mixture was stirred for 12 h at room temperature, then was diluted with
saturated NaHCO3 and brine and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic
extracts were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the crude product by
flash chromatography (hexane : EtOAc = 5 : 1 to 4:1) provided diol 3a.
(1R,2S,E)-2-methy-1-phenylpent-3-ene-1,2-diol (3d). Colorless oil, yield
80%; (1S,2S,E)-2-methy-1-phenylpent-3-ene-1,2-diol (2c);
(p)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-2-(penta-2,3-dien-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane. 3d:
[α ]D 28.0 = 101° (c 0.17 , CHCl3); anti:syn = 10:1; 88% ee; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.28-7.32 (m, 5H), 5.64 (dq, J = 15.6, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 5.49
(dq, J = 15.6, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 4.54 (s, 1H), 2.67 (brs, 1 H), 2.28 (brs, 1
H), 1.69 (dd, J = 6.4, 1.5 Hz, 3H), 1.23 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ ; 139.9, 133.0, 127.8, 127.7, 125.9, 80.8, 75.3, 24.4, 17.9; IR
(neat) 3422, 2972, 1453, 1043, 1026, 973, 750, 702 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z
for C12H16O2Na [M+Na]+ calcd 215.1048, found 215.1047. 2c: [α ]D 28.5 =
-6.50° (c 0.30 , CHCl3); 93% ee; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.28-7.36 (m,
5H), 5.73 (dq, J = 15.5, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 5.55 (dq, J = 15.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H),
4.51 (s, 1H), 2.68 (brs, 1 H), 2.16 (brs, 1 H), 1.72 (dd, J = 6.4, 1.5
Hz, 3H), 1.11 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ ; 139.6, 135.2, 127.8,
127.8, 127.7, 125.4, 79.9, 75.3, 23.0, 17.8; IR (neat) 3413, 3031, 2935,
1495, 1453, 1216, 1042, 1026, 973, 753, 703 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z for
C12H16O2Na [M+Na]+ calcd 215.1048, found 215.1047.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, product depends on temperature (1st
stage), in-situ generated reactant (1st and 2nd stage)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereo- and Enantioselective Synthesis of (E)-2-Methyl-1,2-syn- and
(E)-2-Methyl-1,2-anti-3-pentenediols via Allenylboronate Kinetic
Resolution with (dIpc)2BH and Aldehyde Allylboration
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Jeng-Liang; Chen, Ming; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(12), 3028-3031

