$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-3-(2-(1-hydroxypropyl)phenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (11a). Bromoethane (2.61
g, 24 mmol) was added so slowly to a mixture of Mg (0.6 g, 25 mmol) in
THF (30 ml) that the mixture was kept mild refluxing. After addition, the
mixture was stirred for 2 h. To a solution of
(E)-2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)benzaldehyde (10a) (1.60 g, 10 mmol) in THF
(20 ml) was added a solution of above Grignard reagent (24 mmol) at room
temperature. The reaction solution was stirred for 10 h under refluxing.
After the reaction was cooled to 0 °C, an aqueous saturated solution of
NH4Cl (50 ml) was added dropwise and the resulting mixture was stirred
for 10 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with diethyl ether (40 mL ×
3). The combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuum. The crude residue was purified by chromatography
on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 1/1). Product 11a as yellowish oil
(1.65 g, 86% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.86 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H),
1.70-1.77 (m, 2H), 3.12 (br, 2H), 4.19-4.20 (m, 2H), 4.81 (t, J = 6.8 Hz,
1H), 6.07-6.14 (m, 1H), 6.87 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 7.17-7.26 (m, 2H),
7.36-7.39 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.2, 30.7, 63.2, 72.1,
125.8, 126.4, 127.3, 127.6, 127.8, 130.9, 135.0, 141.2; MS (EI) m/z (rel)
192 (M+, 1), 163 (19), 145 (45), 117 (100), 115 (55), 91 (29), 86 (15),
84 (23), 77 (16); HRMS for C12H16O2: 192.1150; Found: 192.1150; IR
(film): 3344 (br), 2966 (m), 2933 (m), 1875 (m), 1452 (m), 1041 (s), 966
(s), 752 (s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM crude from stage 1 added in stage 2
