$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3. General Procedure (B) for the formation of allylic alcohols:
Benzaldehyde or ketone derivatives were diluted in dry THF (6 mL). The
grignard reagent was added slowly at 0°C. The mixture was stirred 30 min
and allowed to warm to RT. The reaction was monitored by TLC. Following
full consumption of the substrate, the mixture was quenched with a
saturated solution of NH4Cl (10 mL) and extracted with ether (3 x 10 mL).
The combined organic phase was dried over anhydrous MgSO4. Removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure followed by flash column chromatography
(Silica, Eluent: Hexane/AcOEt4/1) afforded the alcohol derivatives.
4-(1-hydroxyallyl)benzonitrile:3 Following the procedure B with
4-formylbenzonitrile 17 (200 mg, 1.53 mmol), vinylmagnesium chloride 1.6
M(1.15 mL, 1.83 mmol) gave the compound (197 mg, 81%) as a pale yellow
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.64 (dt, J = 8.4, 1.7 Hz, 2H, Ar-H),
7.49 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 5.97 (ddd, J = 16.2, 12.4, 3.8 Hz, 1H,
CHCH2),5.37 (dt, J = 17.1; 1.0 Hz, 1H, CH2), 5.23-5.26 (m, 2H, CH2 and
CH-OH); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 147.8, 139.4, 132.4 (2C), 127.0 (2C),
118.9, 116.7, 111.4, 74.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Formation of Allylic Chlorides from Carbonyl Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fuchter, Matthew J.; Levy, Jean-Noel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(21), 4919-4922

