$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The aldehyde (0.277 mmol) and ester (0.554
mmol) were added to a stirred solution of freshly prepared ATNP (0.914
mmol) in toluene (15 mL) at -78 °C (acetone/dry ice bath). After 20
minutes, a stirred solution of LTMP (0.638 mmol) in THF (1.5 mL) at - 78
°C was added via cannula to the ATPH-substrate solution. After 3 hours
following the addition, saturated NH4Cl (15 mL) was added, and the
biphasic mixture was stirred vigorously for 30 minutes while warming to
ambient temperature. The organic phase separated and the aqueous layer
extracted with ether (3 times). The combined organic layers were washed
with brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The reaction mixture was recrystallized from hexanes/chloroform
to remove the majority of 2,6-dinapthalphenol (13). Purification of the
crude product was achieved with flash chromatography (10:1 hexanes:EtOAc
then 3:1 hexanes:EtOAc) to provide the desired product along with
additional recovered 2,6-dinapthalphenol. The combined yield of recovered
2,6-dinapthalphenol was typically above 90%. (E)-methyl
5-hydroxy-5-phenylpent-2-enoate (14) Compound 14 was prepared from
benzaldehyde 13 and methyl crotonate 2 in 97% yield after purification
according to the general procedure. Rf = 0.33 (hexanes/EtOAc 3:1); 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39 - 7.25 (m, 5H), 6.95 (dt, J = 15.6, 7.3 Hz, 1H),
5.89 (dt, J = 15.7, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 4.82 (dd, J = 7.8, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (s,
3H), 2.74 - 2.53 (m, 2H), 2.21 - 1.51 (bs, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
166.91, 145.12, 143.61, 128.90, 128.23, 125.96, 123.91, 73.38, 51.76,
42.08; HRMS (ESI) m/z calc'd for C12H14O3Na [M+Na]+: 229.0841; found:
229.0848.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
