$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):AMD
$DATUM supported on mesoporous silica, complex with copper(II) acetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure of Asymmetric Nitro Aldol
Reaction Asymmetric nitroaldol reactions were carried out in magnetically
stirred screw cap vials under dry and inert conditions. Silica supported
chiral copper (II) complex (108 mg, 0.04 mmol) was added to absolute
ethanol (1 ml) at rt. Reaction mass was stirred after addition of a
chiral imine as an additive (0.1 mmol) and then aldehyde (0.4 mmol) and
nitromethane (0.3 ml, 5.5 mmol) were added to the resulting light green
suspension and stirring was continued for 40 h at rt. The completion of
the reaction was monitored by TLC. The mixture was filtered and the
residue was washed with dry ethanol. The solvent was removed from
combined filtrate and washings and the residue was purified by column
chromatography by using n-hexane/EtOAc (90:10). Enantiomeric excess was
determined by HPLC analysis using chiral column OD, OD-H and AD.8,9 17.
Spectral data of (R)-3-methyl-1-nitro-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-ol 3l: The name
compound was synthesized by using typical procedure and purified by
column chromatography (95:5, n-hexane/EtOAc) to give light yellow oil
(76% yield). FT-IR: 3392, 2972, 2931, 2360, 1943, 1868, 1741, 1696, 1518,
1461, 1395, 1265, 1125, 952, 871, 817, 668 cm-1. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 1.93 (s, 3H), 2.79 (bs, 1H), 4.08-4.11(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 4.54-4.57
(d, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H), 4.90-4.97 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 6.70 (s, 1H),
7.26-7.46 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 11.0, 70.4, 81.4, 128.7,
129.6, 130.1, 133.1, 136.3, 140.9. Anal. calcd. for C11H13NO3: C, 63.76;
H, 6.32; N, 6.76. Found: C, 63.63; H, 6.27; N, 6.80. HPLC analysis:
Chiralcel OD, (85:15, n-hexane:2-propanol, flow 0.8 mL/min) minor
(S)-enantiomer tr = 18.4 min, major (R)-enantiomer tr = 20.9 min. [α]D27
= -9.9° (c = 0.7, CH2Cl2). TOF-MS (ESI+): found C11H13NO3 m/z 208 (M++H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, stereoselective, Henry reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Heterogeneous Chiral Copper Complexes of Amino Alcohol for Asymmetric
Nitroaldol Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mayani, Vishal J.; Abdi, Sayed H. R.; Kureshy, Rukhsana I.; Khan, Noor-ul
H.; Das, Anjan; Bajaj, Hari C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(18), 6191-6195

