$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Allylmagnesium chloride (1.0 M in Et2O, 1.2
equiv) was added dropwise to a stirred solution of the aldehyde (1 equiv)
dissolved in dry Et2O (3 mL/mol) at 0°C. The resulting suspension was
stirred at room temperature overnight and then quenched by addition of
saturated ammonium chloride, extracted with EtOAc (×3). The combined
organic layer was washed with saturated brine (×1), dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and evaporated. The crude products were purified by flash
chromatography. 1-(4-methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (2c). Product 2c was
isolated by flash chromatography (PE:EA = 10:1) in 96% yield as colorless
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.30-7.26 (m, 2H), 6.90-6.86 (m, 2H),
5.85-5.74 (m, 1H), 5.18-5.10 (m, 2H), 4.68 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s,
3H), 2.52-2.47 (m, 2H), 2.04 (br, s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
159.0, 136.1, 134.6, 127.1, 118.2, 113.8, 73.0, 55.3, 43.7.
