$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure 5 for synthesis of allylic alcohols
A solution of aldehyde (100 mol%) in THF (0.10 M with respect to
aldehyde) was cooled to -78°C and Grignard reagent (110 mol%.) added
dropwise. The reaction was then monitored until full consumption of the
aldehyde was observed by TLC. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature and then quenched by the addition a saturated aqueous
solution of NH4Cl (3 × 20 mL/mmol). The mixture was extracted with EtOAc
(3 x 20 ml/mol). The organic layers were combined, dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated. Crude reaction mixture which was purified under the noted
conditions. 1-Phenylhex-5-en-3-ol (1d) Propenyl aldehyde (5.00 g, 37.3
mmol, 4.91 mL) and allyl magnesium bromide (1.0 M in Et2O, 41.0 mmol,
41.0 mL) was subjected to general procedure 5.
1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1e) p-Anisaldehyde (1.00 g, 7.35mmol,
0.893 mL) and allyl magnesium chloride (2.0 M in THF, 8.09 mmol, 4.45 mL)
were subjected to general procedure 5. Alcohol 1e (1.18 g, 90%). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CHLOROFORM-d) δ ppm 7.29 (2 H, d, J=8.6 Hz), 6.89 (2 H, d,
J=8.6 Hz), 5.68-5.90 (1 H, m), 5.05-5.21 (2 H, m), 4.69 (1 H, t, J=6.4
Hz), 3.81 (3 H, s), 2.50 (2 H, t, J=6.8 Hz), 2.07 (1 H, d, J=7.1 Hz). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CHLOROFORM-d) δ ppm 159.0, 136.1, 134.7, 127.1, 118.2,
113.8, 73.0, 55.3, 43.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addition of allyl-MgCl/THF (stage 1), Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM De Novo Synthesis of Multisubstituted Aryl Amines Using Alkene Cross
Metathesis
