$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Alkenols 27-32 (Procedure c). FeCl3 (5 mol %) was added to a mixture of
aldehydes (21-26, 1 equiv) and allyltrimethylsilane (1.1 equiv) in dry
DCM at 0°C. After completion of the reaction as monitored by TLC, the
resulting mixture was quenched with aqueous sodium bicarbonate and
extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and the solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate, 4:1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
