$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Lithiation/Transmetalation/Substitution of
Allyloxy-triethyl-silane (4): Preparation of
(Z)-2-Methyl-1-phenyl-6-(triethyl-silanyloxy)-hexa-1,5-dien-3-ol (5e). A
100 mL round bottom flask (Flask A) with stir bar was flame dried and
charged with BaI2•2H2O (1.656 g, 3.88 mmol) under argon atmosphere. The
flask with the dihydrate was placed in an oil bath and heated to 160
°C-190 °C for 2 hours under high vacuum (0.5-1.0 Torr). In the meantime,
another 100 mL round bottom flask (Flask B) containing a magnetic stir
bar was flame dried under vacuum and flushed with argon. The sealed flask
was cooled to room temperature and then filled with 5 mL of THF. The
solvent and flask are cooled to -78 °C while under a head pressure of
argon. Then, a solution of s-BuLi in cyclohexane (1.3M) was added (872
μL, 1.134 mmol) to the THF solution at -78 °C. This mixture was a bright
yellow and was allowed to cool at -78 °C for 15 minutes. Then a clean 10
mL round bottom flask was charged with the allyl triethylsilyl ether (215
mg, 1.25 mmol). The flask was sealed with a rubber septum, flushed with
argon, and THF (3-5 mL) was added. The resulting solution was added via
syringe pump to the s-BuLi solution in THF slowly over a 15 minutes. The
yellowish color of the s-BuLi in THF disappeared over the course of an
hour to provide a colorless solution at -78 °C. The solution was then
warmed to -40 °C and the deprotonation was allowed to occur for 60-90
minutes with the temperature carefully kept at -40 °C. After 2 hours, the
BaI2 is dry and Flask A was removed from the oil bath, flushed with
argon, and cooled to room temperature. The BaI2 was a white solid after
dehydration and was soluble in THF, albeit slowly. So, to the flask
containing the BaI2, THF (19.40 mL) was added to provide a 0.2M solution
of BaI2 in THF. Upon swirling and much agitation, all of the BaI2 was
solvated providing a transparent (colorless, sometimes pale yellow) 0.2M
solution. After the described deprotonation of allyl triethylsilyl ether
in Flask B, the BaI2 solution in THF (0.2M, 5.67 mL, 1.134 mmol) from
Flask A was added at -78 °C via syringe pump over 15 minutes.
Transmetalation was allowed to proceed for 30 minutes at -78 °C. Then
α-trans-methyl-cinnamaldehyde (83 mg, 0.567 mmol) was added in 1 mL of
THF to Flask B. The resulting solution was colorless and reacted at -78
°C for 10 minutes. Then the reaction mixture was removed from the dry ice
bath and allowed to react for another 10-15 minutes. At this point, the
reaction was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (5 mL) via
syringe and lots of white precipitate was observed in the colorless
reaction mixture. Then 10 mL of water was added to dissolve the inorganic
salts and the mixture was extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 20 mL). The
ethereal extracts were then combined and washed with saturated sodium
thiosulfate (15 mL). The ether was then dried with MgSO4. Rotary
evaporation concentrated the residue and the product was purified using
flash column chromatography with 1:5 (EtOAc:hexanes) as eluent (Rf =
0.15), providing silyl enol ether 5e (180 mg, 80%).
(Z)-2-Methyl-1-phenyl-6-(triethyl-silanyloxy)-hexa-1,5-dien-3-ol (5e).
See the Representative Lithiation/ Transmetalation/Substitution of
Allyloxy-triethyl-silane 4 for the preparation of 5e above, yield (180
mg, 80%). 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 7.35-7.18 (m, 5H), 6.53 (bs,
1H), 6.38 (dt, J = 5.8, 1.4, 1H), 4.53 (td, J = 7.4, 5.8, 1H), 4.23-4.18
(m, 1H), 2.50-2.44 (m, 2H), 2.19 (d, J = 3.7, 1H), 1.88 (d, J = 1.4, 3H),
0.99 (t, J = 8.1, 9H), 0.68 (q, J = 8.1, 6H). 13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm) 140.9, 140.1, 137.9, 129.0, 128.0, 126.2, 125.2, 105.3, 77.5, 30.3,
13.7, 6.5, 4.4. FTIR (cm-1) 3369, 2956, 1656, 1458, 1240, 1114, 1050,
744, 698. HRMS calculated for C19H30O2Si (M-1)+ m/z 317.1937, found
317.1922.
