$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Methoxy-α-(2-propenyl)benzenemethanol, 2b (Table 2, entry 2). An
oven-dried 25 mL round bottom flask was cooled under argon and charged
with (1S,2R)-(+)-2-amino 1,2-diphenylethanol (0.213 g, 1 mmol), indium
powder (0.114 g, 1 mmol), anhydrous THF (7 mL), anhydrous pyridine (0.08
mL, 1 mmol) and allyl bromide (0.084 mL, 2 mmol). The mixture was stirred
vigorously at 25 °C for 30 min, at which time n-hexane (1 mL) was added,
the solution cooled to -78 °C (dry ice/acetone bath), and freshly
distilled p-anisaldehyde (0.06 mL, 0.5 mmol) was added dropwise. After 2
h the reaction was quenched with saturated ammonium chloride (1 mL) and
allowed to warm to 25 °C. Deionized water was added and the mixture
extracted with n-hexane (2 x 3 mL), the combined organic layers were
dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered through a small plug of
silica gel and evaporated to give a clear, colorless oil 2b (0.082 g, 92%
yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.01 (s, 1H, OH), 2.51 (t, J = 6.75
Hz, 2H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 4.71 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (s, 1H), 5.19 (d, J
= 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.73-5.90 (m, 1H), 6.90 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.30 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz, CDCl3): δ): δ 43.8, 55.3, 73.1, 113.8,
118.1, 127.2, 134.8, 136.2, 156.0. Enantiomeric excess was determined to
be 89% by chiral GC analysis. GC conditions: 151 °C isothermal; tR for
the (R)-alcohol: 45.21 min, tR for the (S)-alcohol: 46.10 min.
