$DATUM 60-29-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(2-methylphenyl)hex-5-en-1-ol 38: Magnesium turnings (0.805 g, 33.55
mmol) were added to a dry three necked flask, fitted with a reflux
condenser, dropping funnel and glass stirrer bar and stirred overnight
under a nitrogen atmosphere. Dry diethyl ether (5 ml) was then added to
the turnings, followed by a small amount of 5-bromo-1-pentene (2.4 ml,
20.13 mmol) in diethyl ether (15 ml). The reaction vessel was heated to
reflux. Once Grignard activation was achieved, the remaining
5-bromo-1-pentene was added slowly via the dropping funnel to ensure a
steady reflux. The reaction was stirred until all heat evolution had
ceased (approximately 1 hr), then cooled to 0 °C. o-Tolualdehyde (1.61 g,
13.42 mmol) was dissolved in diethyl ether (10 ml); loaded into the
dropping funnel and added drop wise to the reaction. After complete
addition of the aldehyde, the reaction was allowed to warm to ambient
temperature and stirred for 2 hrs, at which time NMR analysis showed
complete consumption of the aldehyde. The reaction was diluted with a
saturated solution of ammonium chloride (200 ml); left to stir overnight,
then extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 100 ml). The combined organic
extracts were washed with brine (2 x 100 ml) and dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate. The resultant orange residue was subjected to flash
column chromatography (ether/hexane 20:80) to give the alcohol 38 (2.05
g, 81%) as a yellow oil. Rf 0.25 (diethyl ether/hexane 20:80); 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.47 (1H, d, J 7.6, H-6); 7.23 (1H, td, J 1.5, 7.6,
H-5); 7.17 (1H, td, J 7.4, H-4); 7.13 (1H, d, J 7.4, H-3); 5.81 (1H, ddt,
J 6.7, 10.2, 17.0 H-5'); 5.01 (1H, d, J 17.0, H-6'); 4.92-4.97 (2H, m,
H-6'/H-1'); 2.34 (3H, s, -CH3); 2.07-2.14 (2H, m, H-4'); 1.68-1.81(3H, m,
H-2'/-OH); 1.58-1.65 (1H, m, H-3'); 1.42-1.52 (1H, m, H-3'); 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3): δ 143.0 (C-1); 138.6 (C-5'); 134.4 (C-2); 130.4 (C-3); 127.1
(C-4); 126.3 (C-5); 125.1 (C-6); 114.7 (C-6'); 70.6 (C-1'); 37.5 (C-2');
33.6 (C-4'); 25.3 (C-3'); 19.1 (-CH3); IR 3368 (-OH); 3074, 3023, 2975,
2935, 1640 (C=C, alkene); 1603 (C=C, aromatic); 1488, 1459, 1438, 1415,
1380, 1285, 1180, 1064, 994, 910, 756 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd
C13H18NaO [M+Na]+ 213.1255, found 213.1248.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM exothermic reaction stage 1, slow addition of alkenyl bromide stage 1 amd
aldehyde stage 2
