$DATUM [18O]-(±)-1-(4'-Methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (11). A stirred solution of
[18O]-4-methoxybenzaldehyde (250 mg, 1.81 mmol) in dry THF (15 ml) was
cooled to -78°C under nitrogen and treated dropwise with allyl magnesium
chloride (1.09 ml, 2.17 mmol, 2.0 M in THF). The solution was stirred for
1 h and then allowed to reach rt. Further allyl magnesium chloride (1 eq)
was added, and the solution was stirred for 30 min, and then quenched
with water (5 ml). The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (2 x 30 ml), and
the combined organic extracts were washed with brine (30 mI), and dried
(MgSO4). The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to yield the
crude product which was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
eluting with an increasing proportion of ethyl acetate in petrol from 0
to 25% to yield alcohol 11 (245 mg, 75%) as a colorless oil;
[18O]-(±)-1-(4'-Methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (11), Yield 245 mg, 75% ca.
40% 18O as estimated by 13C NMR spectroscopy; silica gel TLC Rf 0.29 (25%
ethyl acetate-petrol); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 2.03 (br, 1 H),
2.47-2.53 (m, 2H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 4.34 (t, J = 6.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.10-5.19 (m,
2H), 5.80 (dddd, J = 17.2, 10.2, 7.1, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 6.86-6.91 (m, 2H),
7.25-7.31 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 43.77,55.30, 72.99 (18O-C),
73.01 (16O-C), 113.84, 118.19, 127.08, 134.63, 136.11, 159.09; MS (CI)
m/z 181 (MH+, 1.2%), 179 (MH+, 2), 161 (17), 137 (34),69 (32), 57 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
