$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (S)-1-arylbut-3-en-1-ols (1).6 A stirred solution of
[(-)-B-chlorodiisopinocampheyl borane] (1.5 eq) in dry THF (25 mL) was
cooled to -78 °C and treated with allyl magnesium chloride (2.0 M in THF,
1.5 eq) under nitrogen. The solution was stirred for 1 h and allowed to
warm to rt over a further 1 h. The solution was cooled to -78 °C and
treated with a solution of aldehyde (1 eq) in dry THF (10 mL). The
solution was stirred for 1 h and allowed to warm to rt over a 1 h. The
solution was treated with a pre-formed mixture of 3.0 M sodium hydroxide
(2.2 eq) and 30% hydrogen peroxide (2.5 eq). After 10 min the mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate (150 mL), washed with water (2 x 50 mL) and
brine (50 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvent evaporated under reduced
pressure to yield the crude product which was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel eluting with an increasing proportion of
ethyl acetate in hexane. (S)-1-(4'-Methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-1-ol ((S)-1b).
4-Methoxybenzaldehyde (1.12 g, 8.22 mmol) was treated according to the
general procedure to yield alcohol (S)-1b as a pale yellow oil (1.06 g,
72%, 89% ee): silica gel TLC Rf 0.29 (25% ethyl acetate-hexane). [α] D22
- 50.7 (c 2.66, CHCl3). (lit.,7 [a] v -27.4 (c 0.5, CHCl3)). Chiral HPLC
(Chiralcel OD-H, 2% IPA/hexane) Rf33.20 min (R-isomer), Rf35.85 min
(S-isomer). Spectral data as previously reported.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
