$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1b)3 Following the
Representative Procedure, 4-methoxybenzaldehyde (136 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexane/MTBE (10:1, 100 mL, 4:1, 100 mL)
provided 1b (127 mg, 71%) as a colorless oil.
1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1b)3, yield 127 mg, 71% Data for 1b: 1H
NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.28 (d, J = 8.8, 2 H, (Aryl)), 6.89 (d, J = 8.8, 2
H, (Aryl)), 5.80 (ddt, J = 17.3, 10.2, 7.2, 1 H, CH(3)), 5.13-5.18 (m, 2
H, H2C(4)), 4.69 (t, J = 6.3, 1 H, HC(1)), 3.81 (s, 3 H, H3C(7')), 2.50
(t, J = 6.8, 2 H, H2C(2)), 2.15 (br, 1 H, (OH)) 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3)
159.0 (C(4')), 136.0 (C(1')), 134.6 (C(3)), 127.0 (C(3'), C(5')), 118.2
(C(4)), 113.7 (C(2'), C(6')), 72.9 (C(7')), 55.2 (C(1)), 43.7 (C(2))IR:
(NaCl) 3411 (m), 3071 (m), 2934 (m), 2836 (m), 1611 (s), 1513 (s), 1465
(m), 1441 (m), 1302 (m), 1247 (s), 1175 (s) HRMS: (CI) Calcd. for
C11H15O2, 179.1072; found, 179.1071 TLC: Rf 0.23 (hexanes/MTBE, 4:1) [UV,
CAM]
