$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the pinacol
cross-coupling reaction To a 10 mL round-bottomed flask was added water
(5 mL), tetrahydrofuran (5 mL), aldehyde (0.5 mmol), α,β-unsaturated
ketone (1 mmol), zinc (1 mmol) and indium trichloride (0.05 mmol)
sequentially, then it was stirred vigorously at room temperature for 5
hours. After reaction, 2 mL HCl (1 M) was added, and then it was
extracted using diethyl ether (20 mL x 3), washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered and evaporated solvent under vacuo to
give the residue. It was subjected to silica gel column chromatography
using ethyl acetate and hexane as eluent to afford the desired product.
2-Methyl-1-phenylbut-3-ene-1,2-diol (3c, Table 2, entry 3): White solid,
yield 76% FTIR (NaCl, neat): ν 3449 (OH) cm−1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3):
(major isomer) δ 1.25 (s, 3H), 2.65 (s, 2H), 4.56 (s, 1H), 5.12-5.20 (m,
2H), 5.79-5.87 (m, 1H), 7.29-7.34 (m, 5H) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3):
(major isomer) δ 142.3 (CH), 140.0 (CH), 139.6 (C), 127.8 (CH), 127.6
(CH), 114.5 (CH2), 80.5 (CH), 75.7 (C), 24.2 (CH3) ppm; HRMS (ESI, m/z):
Calcd. for C11H15O2: 179.1072, found [M+H]+: 179.1070.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, anti:syn 42:58
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Zn/InCl3-Mediated Pinacol Cross-Coupling Reactions of Aldehydes with
α,β-Unsaturated Ketones in Aqueous Media
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yang, Yong-Sheng; Shen, Zhi-Liang; Loh, Teck-Peng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2009), 11(10), 2213-2215

