$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-3-(2-(1-hydroxypropyl)phenyl)-2-methylprop-2-en-1-ol (11d).
Bromoethane (1.63 g, 15 mmol) was added so slowly to a mixture of Mg (384
mg, 15.8 mmol) in THF (30 ml) that the mixture was kept mild refluxing.
After addition, the mixture was stirred for 2 h. To a solution of
(E)-2-(3-hydroxy-2-methylprop-1-enyl)benzaldehyde (10b) (1.10 g, 6.2
mmol) in THF (20 ml) was added a solution of above Grignard reagent (15
mmol) at room temperature. The reaction solution was stirred for 10 h
under refluxing. After the reaction was cooled to 0 °C, an aqueous
saturated solution of NH4Cl (30 ml) was added dropwise and the resulting
mixture was stirred for 10 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with
diethyl ether (30 mL × 3). The combined organic phases were dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuum. The crude residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 1/1).
The product 11d as yellowish oil (1.31 g, 98% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 0.74 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.54 (s, 3H), 1.57-1.66 (m, 2H), 3.17
(br, 1H), 3.52 (br, 1H), 3.99 (s, 2H), 4.63 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 6.51 (s,
1H), 6.99 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.09-7.18 (m, 2H), 7.31-7.33 (m, 1H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.2, 14.8, 30.4, 67.5, 72.4, 122.6, 125.5,
126.7, 126.8, 129.7, 135.7, 138.3, 142.2; MS (EI) m/z (rel) 159 (36), 145
(48), 131 (60), 117 (100), 115 (55), 91 (41), 86 (45), 84 (70); HRMS for
C13H18O2: 206.1307; Found: 206.1309; IR (film): 3323 (br), 2964 (w), 2930
(w), 1446 (m), 1007 (s), 972 (s), 754 (s), 734 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM crude from stage 1 added in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of 2,3-Disubstituted Indanones via
Pd-Catalyzed Intramolecular Asymmetric Allylic Alkylation of Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Xiao-Hui; Zheng, Bao-Hui; Ding, Chang-Hua; Hou, Xue-Long
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(23), 6086-6089

