$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-2, 4-hexadien-1-ol (±)-8o. Method A: Under a nitrogen
atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl compound (14 mmol) in THF (70
mL) was dropwise added the corresponding Grignard or lithium reagents (21
mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room
temperature and stirred until the complete consumption of the substrate.
After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the organic materials were extracted
with EtOAc. The combined organic extract was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1 or (±)-2, using hexadienal (a
mixture of stereoisomers; 1.00 g, 10 mmol), p-MeOC6H4Li generated from
p-MeOC 6H4Br (2.92 g, 16 mmol) and n-BuLi (1.65 M in hexanes; 9.50 mL, 16
mmol), and THF (34 mL). After 1.5 h at room temperature, work-up and
column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 10:1 to 5:1) gave (±)-8o (a
mixture of stereoisomers; 1.95 g, 92%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.32-7.27 (m, 2H), 6.90-6.86 (m, 2H), 6.62 (dd, J= 15.0,
11.0 Hz, 0.11H), 6.25 (dd, J= 15.0, 10.5 Hz, 0.89H), 6.11-5.99 (m, 1H),
5.83 (dd, J= 15.0, 6.5 Hz, 0.11H), 5.78-5.69 (m, 1.78H), 5.58-5.50 (m,
0.11H), 5.24 (dd, J= 6.3, 4.0 Hz, 0.11H), 5.18 (dd, J= 6.3, 3.5 Hz,
0.89H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 1.86 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 0.89H), 1.77 (dd, J= 6.3, 1.8
Hz, 0.33H), 1.75 (d, J= 6.3 Hz, 2.67H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
159.1, 135.3, 132.5, 130.8, 130.7, 130.4, 127.5, 113.9, 74.4, 55.3, 18.2.
IR (CHCl3) ν: 3599 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C13H15O [M-OH]+:
187.1117. Found: 187.1134.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Optically Active Allyl Esters via Lipase-Vanadium
Combo Catalysis
