$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-3-phenylpropanenitrile (19f). Purification by
column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound 19f
(158 mg, 99%) as a viscous liquid. Spectral data were identical to those
previously reported.6 TLC: R f 0.22 (3:1 hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.42-7.37 (m, 5H), 6.13 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 6.06 (d, 1H, J =
1.6 Hz), 5.33 (m, 1H), 2.24 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 139.3, 130.1, 129.1, 129.1, 126.7, 126.3, 117.1, 74.2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium triflimide as solvent
gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
