$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1) Standard Procedure for the Synthesis of α,β- Epoxyketone. Synthesis
of 1-(4-Methoxy-phenyl)-prop-2-en-1-ol. To a THF (10 mL) solution of
p-methoxyphenyl aldehyde (2.00 g, 14.7 mmol) was added vinylmagnesium
bromide (17.6 mL, 1 M, 17.6 mmol) at 0 °C, and the mixture was stirred
for 2 h before addition of H2O. The solution was evaporated under reduced
pressure, and the organic layer was extracted with diethyl ether. The
extract was dried in vacuo and chromatographed through a silica column to
give allylic alcohol as a colorless oil (1.98 g, 12.0 mmol, 82%). IR
(neat, cm-1): 3423 (vs, br), 1645 (m), 1614 (w). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 7.28 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.07-5.99 (m, 1H),
5.33 (dd, J = 17.6, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.16 (dd, J = 12.8, 1.5 Hz), 5.14 (s,
1H), 3.78 (s, 3H), 1.94 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 159.0,
140.3, 134.8, 127.6, 114.6, 113.8, 74.7, 55.2. HRMS (70 eV): calcd for
C10H12O2, 164.0837; found, 164.0836.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Highly Efficient Ruthenium-Catalyzed Rearrangement of α,β-Epoxyketones
to 1,2-Diketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chang, Chia-Lung; Kumar, Manyam Praveen; Liu, Rai-Shung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(8), 2793-2796

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME259 STEP1
$RXN



  2  1
$MOL
