$DATUM (S)-Alcohol 17: 4-Chlorobenzaldehyde (4.0 g, 28.5 mmol) was subjected to
Keck's asymmetric allylation conditions to afford 5.13 g (99%, 95% ee) of
alcohol 17: [α]23 D -56.2° (c 0.60, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.3 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.24 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2 H), 5.75 (m, 1 H) 5.12
(m, 2 H), 4.65 (t, J = 5.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.45 (m, 2 H), 1.92 (bs, 1 H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.3, 133.9, 133.0, 128.4, 127.1, 118.6, 72.5,
43.7. The optical purity of this material was determined by HPLC analysis
of the corresponding Mosher's esters (Chiracel-OD-H, 98 : 2, hexane :
isopropanol, Rt = 6.3 min (R--alcohol-(R)-MPTA), 6.8 min
(S--alcohol-(R)-MPTA).
