$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure F for allylation of
aldehydes and sulfonimides: Tributylstannane (0.155 mL, 0.5 mmol, 2
equiv.) was added to a mixture of sulfonimides (0.25 mmol, 1 equiv.) or
aldehydes (0.25 mmol, 1 equiv.) and POM 3a (53 mg, 0.01 mmol, 4.0 mol %)
dissolved in 0.5 mL of DMF in a sealed microwave vial containing a stir
bar. The mixture was stirred and heated to 40 °C under MW for 1 hour. The
solvent was evaporated and the crude material was purified by column
chromatography. N-(1-phenylbut-3-enyl)benzenesulfonamide 6a: Prepared
according to general procedure F from (E)-N-benzylidenebenzenesulfonamide
(61 mg, 0.25 mmol). The crude material was purified by column
chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc: 90/10).
1-(4-chlorophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol 7c: Prepared according to general
procedure F from 4- chlorobenzaldehyde (35 mg, 0.25 mmol). The crude
material was purified by column chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc:
90/10). The alcool 7c as a yellow solid (32 mg, 0.18 mmol, 71% yield). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.33-7.28 (m, 4H, arom.), 5.83-5.73 (m, 1H,
CH2-CH=CH2), 5.18-5.14 (m, 2H, CH2-CH=CH2), 4.74-4.71 (m, 1H, CHOH),
2.54-2.43 (m, 2H, CH2-CH=CH2), 2.08 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H, CHOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, sealed tube used
