concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash column
chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc 8:1) to give the known homoallyl alcohol
8a1 (106 mg, 93%) as a colorless oil. The reaction was repeated one more
time and the product was isolated in 95% yield.
