$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Palladium-Catalyzed Allylation of Aldehydes by
Pincer Complex Catalysts. Representative procedure for the allylation of
p-bromobenzaldehyde with allyltributyltin in the presence of complex 1: A
dried Schlenk was charged with p-bromo benzaldehyde (92.5 mg, 0.5 mmol),
complex 1 (4.4 mg, 0.0050 mmol, 1.0 mol %), and THF (0.5 mL) under
nitrogen. Allyl tributyltin (186μL, 0.6 mmol) was then added via syringe.
The resulting solution was stirred at the desired temperature for 24 h.
Thereafter the reaction mixture was evaporated, diluted into water, and
extracted with ether. The organic layer was separated, washed with brine,
dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated. The crude product was then purified by
flash column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc) to give the homoallylic
alcohol as a colorless oil. The NMR data obtained for the coupling
products are in agreement with the corresponding literature. 37,78
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Joint Experimental and Theoretical Study of the Palladium-Catalyzed
Electrophilic Allylation of Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Piechaczyk, Olivier; Cantat, Thibault; Mezailles, Nicolas; Le Floch,
Pascal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(11), 4228-4237

