$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Allylboration of aldehydes using Soderquist’s
10-TMS-borabicyclo[3.3.2]- decane: Preparation of
1-(4-bromophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (4e). In a flame dried 100mL roundbottom
flask under N2, 9-(1R,2R-Pseudoephedrinyl)-(10S)-(trimethylsilyl)-9-
borabicyclo[3.3.2]decane (4.8g, 12.97mmol) prepared according to
literature precedent, was dissolved in dry Et2O and cooled to -78°C. To
this solution, allylmagnesium bromide (12.9mL, 1M in Et2O) was added; the
suspension was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 1h. The white
suspension was cooled to -78°C. 4-bromobenzaldehyde (2.0g, 10.81mmol) was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 and added to the suspension slowly along the inside
of the flask. The reaction was stirred at -78°C for 3h. The flask was
warmed to room temperature and the solvent removed under reduced
pressure. The pasty white solids were suspended in pentane and filtered
through a pad of Celite. The pad was washed with pentane and the solvent
removed under reduced pressure. The colorless oil was dissolved in dry
acetonitrile (18mL) and 1R,2R-pseudoephedrine (2.14g, 12.97mmol) was
added. The flask was purged with N2, fitted with a reflux condenser and
refluxed for 2h. The solution was cooled to room temperature and
colorless large crystals formed. The crystals were collected, rinsed with
hexanes (3.14g 65% recovered) and the filtrate was rotovapped. The
residue was subjected to column chromatography (5:1 hexanes/Et2O) to
provide 4e in 88% as a colorless oil. Spectral data for 4e agrees with
literature (Yanagisawa, A.; Nakashima, H.; Yamamoto, H. J. Am. Chem. Soc.
1996, 118(19), 4723.). 1-(4-bromophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (4e): 4e was
isolated in 88% yield as a colorless oil.
