$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Allylation of
Aldehydes. To a suspension of p-nitrobenzoic acid (84 mg, 0.5 mmol) in
acetonitrile (1.5 mL) were added successively benzaldehyde (53 mg, 0.5
mmol) and allyltributyltin (198 mg, 0.6 mmol) at room temperature. After
being stirred about 3 h, the solution turned clear. The reaction was
quenched with HCl (2 M, 2 mL) after completion (23 h), then filtered and
washed with CH2Cl2 (2 × 5 mL) to recover p-nitrobenzoic acid (80 mg,
95%). The filtrate (aqueous layer) was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 5 mL).
The combined organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure to furnish the crude product, which was purified by
silica gel chromatography (typical eluent: petroleum ether/EtOAc 14:1
(v/v)) to afford 3a (73 mg, 99%). 1-(3-methoxyphenyl)-3-penten-1-ol (6c)
(Z-isomer)16 2-methyl-1-(3-methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (7c) 19
1-(3-methoxyphenyl)-3-penten-1-ol (6c) (Z-isomer)16 1H NMR (300MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.28-7.23(m, 1H), 6.95-6.93(m, 2H), 6.83-6.79(m, 1H),
5.67-5.61(m, 1H), 5.47-5.40(m, 1H), 4.71-4.66(m, 1H), 3.81(s, 3H),
2.59-2.43(m, 2H), 2.09(d, 1H, J = 2.8 Hz), 1.60(d, 3H, J = 7.5 Hz); IR
(KBr, film): υ 3421, 2939, 2836, 1655, 1602, 1586, 1488, 1260, 1044, 874,
701 cm-1. 2-methyl-1-(3-methoxyphenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (7c) 19 syn/anti =
60/40. 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.28-7.21(m, 1H), 6.94-6.79(m, 3H),
5.83-5.71(m, 1H), 5.22-5.16(m, 1x 0.4H)(anti), 5.08-5.03(m, 1x
0.6H)(syn), 4.57(d, 1x 0.6H, J = 4.3 Hz)(syn), 4.31(d, 1x 0.4H, J = 7.5
Hz)(anti), 3.80(s, 3H), 2.58-2.46(m, 1H), 2.19(s, 1x 0.4 H)(anti),
2.01(s, 1x 0.6H)(syn), 0.99(d, 3x 0.6Hz, J = 6.9 Hz)(syn), 0.86(d, 3x
0.4H, J = 7.0 Hz)(anti); IR (KBr, film): υ 3436, 3078, 2964, 2935, 2836,
1638, 1602, 1586, 1455, 1260, 1042, 915, 703 cm-1.
