$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Rhodium-Catalyzed
Reductive Allylation of Conjugated Aldehydes with Allyl Acetate. A glass
liner containing the substrate (2 mmol), [Rh(TMEDA)(CO)2][RhCl2(CO)2] (5
mol %), Cs2CO3 nH2O (2 mmol), allyl acetate (8 mmol) and THF (10 mL) was
placed in a 45 mL autoclave equipped with a magnetic stirring bar. The
autoclave was flushed three times with carbon monoxide and then
pressurized to 10 bar. The autoclave was placed in an oil bath preset to
100°C (110°C)* on a stirring hot plate. After 24 h (72 h)*, the autoclave
was removed from the oil bath and cooled to room temperature prior to the
release of CO gas. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuum, and
the residue was purified by flash chromatography using 20% of ethyl
acetate in hexanes as eluant to afford the product.
1-(4-Bromophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (3h)6: The crude compound was purified by
flash chromatography with 20% of EtOAc in hexanes used as eluant to
obtain the title compound as a pale-yellow oil in 83% yield 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ ppm 2.30 (bs, 1H), 2.52 - 2.4 (m, 2H), 4.67 (t, J = 6.55, 1H),
5.18 - 5.12 (m, 2H), 5.82 - 5.71 (m, 1H), 7.22 (d, J = 8.15, 2H), 7.47
(d, J = 8.16, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm 43.70, 72.51, 118.75, 121.16,
127.5, 131.38, 133.87, 142.75; m/z (EI) 228 ([M]+ 0.3%), 187 ([M - C3H5]+
92), 185 ([M - C3H5]+ 100), 159 (15), 157 (21), 77 (76), 51 (14).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhodium-Catalyzed Reductive Allylation of Conjugated Aldehydes with Allyl
Acetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Vasylyev, Maksym; Alper, Howard
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(8), 2710-2713

