$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diethyl zinc (1.1 M in toluene, 55 μL, 0.06 mmol) was charged to an
anhydrous solution of borolanes 12 and 6 (91 : 9 of borolanes 12 and 6,
300 mg, 1.8 mmol) and pmethoxybenzaldehyde (0.15 mL, 168 mg, 1.2 mmol) in
toluene (6 mL) under argon at 0°C. The homogeneous solution was agitated
at 0 οC for 18 h. HPLC analysis of the reaction solution at 18 h showed
99 : 1 site selectivity between propargyl 5a and allenylic 4a alcohols by
comparison to reference standards of allenyl and homopropargylic
alcohols.1 The reaction was warmed to ambient temperature and treated
with diethanolamine (0.35 mL). The reaction mixture was agitated for 1 h
at ambient temperature. The reaction was diluted with isopropyl acetate
(10 mL) and washed with water (3 x 10 mL). The organic portion was
concentrated to an oil. Purification by silica gel chromatography (10-20
% EtOAc in hexanes) provided the propargylic alcohol 5a. A slightly
yellow oil (200 mg, 92 %).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Zinc-Catalyzed Allenylations of Aldehydes and Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fandrick, Daniel R.; Saha, Jaideep; Fandrick, Keith R.; Sanyal, Sanjit;
